The Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm is an efficient method for generating prime numbers up to a given limit. It works by iteratively marking the multiples of each prime number, starting from 2, as composite (not prime). By the end of the algorithm, all remaining numbers in the list are prime.

To implement this algorithm recursively, you can create a recursive function that takes a number as input and returns whether it is prime or not. The function can then be used to generate the array of prime numbers by recursively checking each number from 2 to 100.

